        <!-- what trained models do with the bands -->
        <h3 class="sub-h">
          <span class="lang-en">What trained models put on the bands — Barbero et al. (2410.06205)</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">학습된 모델은 band에 무엇을 싣는가 — Barbero et al. (2410.06205)</span>
        </h3>
        <div class="card-grid barb-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Observed: norms pile onto slow dials</span><span class="lang-ko">관측: norm은 느린 다이얼에 쌓인다</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">In pretrained Gemma 7B, training "has assigned much
                higher norm on average to the lowest frequencies" — which, by the cosine
                series above, means they "influence the dot product the most … at each
                layer"; the authors "suspect they are used to carry semantic information."
                High-frequency usage appears "especially at the very first and last layers."
                This is observational analysis of a trained model, not an intervention.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">pretrained Gemma 7B에서 학습은 "가장 낮은 frequency에
                평균적으로 훨씬 높은 norm을 할당"했다 — 위 cosine 급수에 따르면 이는 매
                layer에서 dot product에 가장 크게 기여한다는 뜻이고, 저자들은 이 band가
                "semantic 정보를 나른다"고 본다. high-frequency 사용은 "특히 첫 layer와
                마지막 layer에서" 나타난다. 학습된 모델에 대한 관측 분석이며 개입 실험이
                아니다.</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">Gemma 7B · per-band 2-norm analysis</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Observed: fast dials build positional heads</span><span class="lang-ko">관측: 빠른 다이얼은 positional head를 만든다</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">Gemma 7B "learns to use RoPE to construct robust
                'positional' attention patterns by exploiting the highest frequencies": a
                diagonal head in the last layer (L27 H8, mostly high-frequency by their
                Fig. 6), a previous-token head in the first layer, and an apostrophe-detector
                head that is both semantic and positional. Theory to match: a RoPE head can
                express pure positional selection and diagonal/off-diagonal patterns
                (Prop. 3.1, Thm 5.3) where a NoPE head cannot (Prop. 5.2) — but with
                low-but-nonzero frequencies, a head eventually fails to attend robustly to a
                semantic target as context grows (Thm 6.1): slow-but-moving dials misalign,
                motivating huge bases or truncation.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">Gemma 7B는 "가장 높은 frequency를 이용해 견고한
                'positional' attention 패턴을 구성하도록 학습"된다: 마지막 layer의 diagonal
                head(L27 H8, Fig. 6 기준 대부분 high-frequency), 첫 layer의 previous-token
                head, 그리고 semantic과 positional을 겸하는 apostrophe 검출 head. 이론도
                맞물린다: RoPE head는 순수 positional 선택과 diagonal/off-diagonal 패턴을
                표현할 수 있지만(Prop. 3.1, Thm 5.3) NoPE head는 불가능하다(Prop. 5.2).
                다만 0이 아닌 낮은 frequency는 context가 커지면 semantic 표적에 견고하게
                attend하지 못하게 된다(Thm 6.1) — 느리지만 도는 다이얼은 결국 어긋나고,
                거대한 base 혹은 truncation의 동기가 된다.</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">Fig. 5–6 · Prop. 3.1 · Thm 5.3 / 6.1</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="prope-panel">
