      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ f · SYSTEMS CORNER ============ -->
    <section class="section-tight" id="systems">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="viz-h">
          <span class="lang-en">f · Systems corner — where the rotation meets the cache</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">f · Systems corner — 회전이 cache를 만나는 곳</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="viz-sub">
          <span class="lang-en">Three published designs that exist because of section a's
            two facts: K is cached post-RoPE, and position lives only in the q·k score.
            Published claims only.</span>
          <span class="lang-ko">section a의 두 사실 — K는 post-RoPE로 cache되고, position은
            q·k score에만 산다 — 때문에 존재하는 세 가지 공개된 설계. 공개된 주장만
            담았다.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="card-grid sys-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3><span class="lang-en">Rotate-at-write</span><span class="lang-ko">Rotate-at-write</span> <span class="to-year">HF transformers</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">In the standard HF path, apply_rotary_pos_emb runs
                before past_key_values.update(...) — verified code order in
                modeling_qwen3.py. Every cached K is therefore stamped with the position it
                was written at: a cached entry cannot be reused at a different position
                without un-rotating and re-rotating it. vLLM's rotary layer follows the same
                rotate-before-write convention (its rotary implementations verified; the
                cache-write ordering itself is the standard reading).</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">표준 HF 경로에서 apply_rotary_pos_emb는
                past_key_values.update(...)보다 먼저 실행된다 — modeling_qwen3.py에서
                검증한 코드 순서다. 따라서 cache된 모든 K에는 쓰인 시점의 position이
                새겨져 있다: cache 항목을 다른 position에서 재사용하려면 회전을 풀고 다시
                돌려야 한다. vLLM의 rotary layer도 같은 rotate-before-write 관례를 따른다
                (rotary 구현은 검증됨; cache 쓰기 순서 자체는 표준적 해석).</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">q_norm → RoPE → cache update — verified order</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3><span class="lang-en">MLA — position as a side-channel</span><span class="lang-ko">MLA — side-channel로 옮긴 position</span> <span class="to-year">DeepSeek-V2 · 2405.04434</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">Low-rank absorbed keys can't carry RoPE: "W^UK … will be
                coupled with a position-sensitive RoPE matrix … [and] cannot be absorbed
                into W^Q any more during inference." DeepSeek-V2's fix is decoupled RoPE:
                per-head rotary queries plus ONE shared 64-dim rotary key per token
                (d_h^R = 64), cached alongside the 512-dim latent — position lives only in
                the 64-dim side-channel; the 512-dim latent is position-free by
                construction. Full walkthrough in the
                <a href="/study/models/attention-anatomy/">attention-anatomy deep-dive</a>.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">low-rank로 흡수된 key는 RoPE를 실을 수 없다: "W^UK는
                position에 민감한 RoPE 행렬과 결합되어 … inference에서 더 이상 W^Q에
                흡수될 수 없다." DeepSeek-V2의 해법이 decoupled RoPE다: head별 rotary
                query와, token당 하나의 공유 64-dim rotary key(d_h^R = 64)를 512-dim
                latent 옆에 cache한다 — position은 64-dim side-channel에만 살고, 512-dim
                latent는 구조적으로 position-free다. 전체 과정은
                <a href="/study/models/attention-anatomy/">attention-anatomy 딥다이브</a>
                참고.</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">cache = 512 position-free + 64 rotated</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3><span class="lang-en">KVQuant — quantize before the rotation</span><span class="lang-ko">KVQuant — 회전 전에 quantize</span> <span class="to-year">Hooper et al. · 2401.18079</span></h3>
            <p>
              <span class="lang-en">Published rationale: keys "pre-RoPE exhibit clear
                outliers in specific channels across different tokens", while "after
                applying RoPE, the distribution becomes less structured … (this is expected,
                as RoPE applies a rotation operation between pairs of channels)." Their
                scheme quantizes keys pre-RoPE and applies the rotation on-the-fly after
                dequantization with a fused kernel — a claimed 0.82 perplexity improvement
                on Wikitext-2 for 3-bit LLaMA-7B versus post-RoPE per-channel quantization,
                "without adding runtime overhead" (their claim). See the
                <a href="/reviews/kvquant/">KVQuant review</a>.</span>
              <span class="lang-ko">공개된 논거: key는 "pre-RoPE에서 token이 달라도 특정
                channel에 뚜렷한 outlier"를 보이는 반면, "RoPE 적용 후에는 분포가 덜
                구조적이 된다 … (RoPE가 channel pair 사이에 회전을 가하므로 예상되는
                일이다)." 이들의 방식은 key를 pre-RoPE로 quantize하고, dequantization 후
                fused kernel로 회전을 on-the-fly 적용한다 — 3-bit LLaMA-7B에서 post-RoPE
                per-channel quantization 대비 Wikitext-2 perplexity 0.82 개선을 주장하며,
                "runtime overhead 추가 없이"라는 것도 저자들의 주장이다.
                <a href="/reviews/kvquant/">KVQuant 리뷰</a> 참고.</span>
            </p>
            <span class="ev-chip">quantize pre-RoPE → dequant → rotate on read</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

